      notes: 'LINH: Have you finished the price list yet? The customer has just asked for it again. ADAM: I’ve already updated the prices, but I haven’t checked the delivery dates yet. Have you heard from the supplier? LINH: Yes. They sent me a message at nine this morning. Two items won’t arrive until Friday. ADAM: Okay. I’ve changed the dates for those items now. Have you worked with this supplier before? LINH: Yes, several times. We first used them last year, and they solved a delivery problem for us in June. ADAM: That’s good. I’ve never dealt with them directly. Did you call them about the delay this morning? LINH: Yes, I did. They explained the reason and offered another delivery option. I’ve just forwarded the message to you. ADAM: Thanks. I can see it now. I’ve checked all the dates, so the list is ready. Who should I send it to? LINH: Send it to Ms. Hoa, please. She emailed us yesterday. I haven’t replied to her yet. ADAM: All right. I’ll send the list now, and you can reply to her questions. Let’s check again before lunch.',
